<%# The tinted left half of the login screen: a product shot above the promise
    of having an account.

    The mockup asks for a lifestyle shot here. The project has one image,
    already used by the home hero, so it is reused rather than left as an empty
    slot — the panel reads as finished either way, since the copy carries it.

    Included by pages/login.ejs. Takes no locals. %>
<div class="auth-panel">
  <%# Decorative: the heading below says everything this image says, so an alt
      text would only repeat it to a screen reader. %>
  <img src="/img/hero-product.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" class="auth-panel__image" />

  <div>
    <h2 class="auth-panel__title">
      Your desk setup, saved to your account.
    </h2>
    <p class="auth-panel__text">
      Track orders, save Mashup builds and get early access to new peripherals.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
